CORE
F12ModifiesTest
--function F12ModifiesTest.caller --modular -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
type inconsistency
falling back to inlining
--
The JVerify `modifies(target)` write-frame clause is mapped by
java_bytecode_contracts onto the c_assigns frame (same as `assigns`).
The direct-argument capture path unwraps autoboxing so a primitive
field target (`modifies(counter)`) resolves to the field lvalue rather
than the boxed Integer temporary, so DFCC accepts it and modular
substitution applies WITHOUT falling back to inlining.
